    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17620" root="زر" body-key="z">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زُرْزُورٌ</span></b>  [The <i>starling;</i>] <i>a certain bird,</i> (IDrd, S,
O, K,) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زُرْزُرٌ</span></b> , (IDrd, O, K,) <i>resembling
the lark:</i> pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَرَازِيرُ</span>. (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرْكَبٌ زُرْزُورٌ</span> <i>A
narrow</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مركب</span> [or <i>animal,</i> or <i>thing, upon which
one rides</i> or <i>is carried;</i> accord. to the TK, meaning a <i>beast;</i> for it is there added that one says

<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حِمَارٌ زُرْزُورٌ</span>, meaning <i>a narrow ass</i>]. (O, K. *) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زُرْزُورُ مَالٍ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زِرٌّ</span> last sentence but one.

